{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user is asking me to implement a `solve(case)` function for task AGENT-TF-01. Let me analyze the requirements carefully.\n\nFrom the fixture data and the candidate artifact description, I need to implement a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism.\n\nThe key steps are:\n1. For each call, compute gain = `loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by dividing by `prediction_tokens` (at least 1)\n3. Accept a call if it is `parseable` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` and `diagnostics` in the original order\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.48911432, loss_with=0.30132987, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445\n  - normalized_gain = 1.18778445 / 5 = 0.23755689\n  - accepted = true (parseable=true, normalized_gain \u003e= 0.05)\n- call1: loss_without=1.37006381, loss_with=0.10127803, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.26878578\n  - normalized_gain = 0.25375716\n  - accepted = true\n- call2: loss_without=1.07992348, loss_with=0.04054692, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.03937656\n  - normalized_gain = 0.20787531\n  - accepted = true\n- call3: loss_without=1.76582941, loss_with=0.57732788, tokens=3, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.18850153\n  - normalized_gain = 0.39616718\n  - accepted = true\n- call4: loss_without=1.70674574, loss_with=0.40289862, tokens=6, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.30384712\n  - normalized_gain = 0.21730785\n  - accepted = true\n- call5: loss_without=1.98682122, loss_with=0.89260518, tokens=4, parseable=false\n  - gain = 1.09421604\n  - normalized_gain = 0.27355401\n  - accepted = false (not parseable)\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call4\"]\n\nThe schema says `normalized_gain` is a number. The artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out the rounding. Let me think about reasonable rounding - maybe to some decimal places. The schema just says \"number\" so perhaps rounding to a few decimal places makes sense.\n\nLooking at the description: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - I'll round normalized_gain to perhaps 8 decimal places or maybe the standard Python round to some sensible precision.\n\nActually, given the fixture values have 8 decimal places, I'll round to 8 decimal places to be safe.\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Normalize by at least 1 prediction token\n        denom = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / denom\n        \n        # Round normalized gain\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        # Accept if parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain_rounded \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Now I need to format it as a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me write the final JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        # Normalize by at least 1 prediction token\\n        denom = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / denom, 8)\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01183U04IvqvHhaLhy7BBKQo","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2350},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2350,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1388,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1090},"service_tier":"standard"}}